<title>UK: UK's Crestco to press on with April conversion.</title>
<headline>UK's Crestco to press on with April conversion.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The board of CrestCo, the operator of a computerised share registration system for the London market, decided unanimously to stick to its timetable for full conversion to paperless share trading, the Times said.</p>
<p>CrestCo claimed the proportion of UK equities settling in Crest had risen to 40 percent from 25 percent since November 6. The number of deals settling on time had increased to 70 percent from 60 percent, the paper said. This falls short of Talisman though  -- which Crest supercedes -- which settles 79 percent of trades to schedule, the Times said.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
